I doubt they will turn up.  I and at least two other people went through al=
l those boxes, alphabetized them and checked that replies were sent to ques=
tions. =20
JCB talked Loglan a lot when I was around ( and several others report the s=
ame) but that was all before the great morphological revolution.  I don't k=
now about after that.  As to how fluent he was,I can't say, since I could n=
ot keep up with him.  I assume whatever he said meant what he intended by f=
iat.
The textbooks never got beyond drafts, very primitive programmed texts of v=
ery primitive parts, while I was there (1984).

Sent from my iPad

